description.narrative:
The ending of the Chemicals management project in Serbia marks the finalization of 13 years of chemicals cooperation between the Swedish Chemicals Agency and the Serbian Ministry of Environmental Protection (former Ministry of Agriculture and Environmental Protection). The last phase of the cooperation took place between 2016 -2022, and contributed to the progress in implementation and enforcement of the adopted chemicals legislation in Serbia. 
The project objective was to support effective implementation of the EU aquis (legislation) on chemicals and biocidal products, supporting legislation alignment, and preparations of legislation as well as the establishment of adequate institutional capacities. Examples of results are;
1) the establishment of a chemicals e-reporting system used by authorities and industry to provide and exchange information strengthening reporting and enforcement of legislation (used by more than 1100 different companies), capacities and technical systems have been built;
2) necessary amendments made to the law on chemicals and the law on biocidal products, drafted legal documents are aligned with EU standards and agreed to be adopted;
3) a large number of chemicals inspectors are fully trained and prepared as competent authorities under EU chemicals legislation;
The e-portals and e-reporting systems supported by the project directly contributed to the goal of the Government of the Republic of Serbia on digitalization of the public administrative procedures.
